&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Digital Assets Security Engineer to own security for Alpaca&#39;s crypto and tokenization products. The scope includes custody and key management, transaction authorization policies, secure engineering for wallets and tokenization, and monitoring of high-risk asset movements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Several of the largest digital asset thefts in recent years started with a compromised signer, a manipulated signing screen, or social engineering of the people who approve transactions. This role focuses on those paths: who can move assets, under what policy, and what approvers see before they sign. You will work in both the engineering details and the governance around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the CISO and works closely with the crypto and tokenization engineering teams, Crypto Operations, Compliance, GRC, and the wider Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security Team is 100% distributed and remote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The core responsibilities of the Digital Assets Security Engineer are focused on custody and key security, transaction authorization and governance, secure engineering for crypto and tokenization, and monitoring and response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custody and Key Security:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custody Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the security design of wallets, vaults, and signing infrastructure across hot, warm, and cold storage, including MPC and HSM configuration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Lifecycle:&lt;/strong&gt; Set requirements for key generation, backup, recovery, rotation, and destruction. Run or oversee key ceremonies and recovery tests with Crypto Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Signing Integrity:&lt;/strong&gt; Secure the path from a transaction request to a signature, including API credentials, co-signers, approval devices, and what approvers see before they sign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transaction Authorization and Governance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transaction Policies:&lt;/strong&gt; Review transaction authorization policies, such as Fireblocks TAP, including approval quorums, amount thresholds, destination allowlists, and velocity limits. Recommend changes to Crypto Operations and Compliance, who own and approve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Advise on how changes to policies, admins, signers, and allowlisted addresses are proposed, approved, and applied. Confirm every change leaves a reviewable record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access Reviews:&lt;/strong&gt; Review admin, signer, approver, and API user access on custody platforms on a set schedule, and flag access that is no longer needed for removal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Third-Party Risk:&lt;/strong&gt; Assess custody providers, node and RPC providers, token issuers, and other digital asset vendors with Cyber GRC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards and Evidence:&lt;/strong&gt; In collaboration with the Cyber GRC team, write the security standards for digital asset operations, and provide technical evidence for audits and regulatory exams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Engineering for Crypto and Tokenization:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Reviews:&lt;/strong&gt; Review architecture and code changes for wallet services, custody integrations, blockchain node infrastructure, and tokenization flows. Give engineers clear, practical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Threat model minting, redemption, transfers, settlement, and reconciliation between on-chain balances and internal books and records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Smart Contract Review:&lt;/strong&gt; Review token contracts and issuer controls, such as mint and burn authority, upgradeability, admin keys, and freeze functions, for tokens we support or integrate with.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service Identity and Secrets:&lt;/strong&gt; Set requirements for how services authenticate to custody platforms, including HSM-backed signing keys, scoped API credentials, and least-privilege service accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitoring and Response:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detection:&lt;/strong&gt; Define alerts for high-risk activity, such as policy and admin changes, new destination addresses, unusual withdrawals, and signer changes. Work with Security Operations to build and tune them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Chain Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor the addresses and contracts Alpaca depends on for suspicious activity, with Security Operations and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Response:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the digital asset side of security incidents, including suspected key compromise, unauthorized transfers, and malicious approvals. Maintain playbooks to freeze, rotate, and recover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Call:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in the Security on-call rotation after onboarding and cross-training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about Alpaca&#39;s mission and what we&#39;re building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in security engineering, including 2+ years securing digital asset, crypto, or blockchain systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with institutional custody, such as MPC or HSM-backed wallets, key backup and recovery, and policy-based transaction controls (Fireblocks,Turnkey, BitGo, Copper, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or reviewing transaction authorization policies, including approval quorums, amount thresholds, address allowlists, and separation of initiators, approvers, and signers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of how transactions and signatures work on EVM chains and Solana, including token standards, token approvals, nonces, and finality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear understanding of how digital asset theft happens in practice: signer device compromise, blind signing, social engineering of operators, address poisoning, malicious token approvals, and key exfiltration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read code and design documents well enough to challenge implementation choices, with programming experience in Python, Go, TypeScript, Rust, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud security, service identity, secrets management, and KMS or HSM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing security standards and producing control evidence for auditors or regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, especially when explaining risk to engineers, operators, and compliance partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to participate in an on-call rotation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing broker-dealers, exchanges, custodians, money services businesses, or other regulated financial platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Smart contract security review experience (Solidity or Rust) with tools such as Foundry, Slither, or Echidna&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tokenized securities, stablecoins, or on-chain settlement and reconciliation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running key ceremonies or designing custody recovery and disaster recovery procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with blockchain analytics and on-chain monitoring tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance security rigor with operational efficiency and business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
